 },
 "label": "pre-specified later analysis (test numbers read after the v7 rule was registered)",
 "item": "A5_multi_positive_sensitivity",
 "definition": {
  "type": "code reading + pre-specified sensitivity",
  "question": "Are other true same-timestamp answers treated as negatives in Eq. (4)?",
  "rule": "if they are NOT masked: fit a masked-denominator variant on polecat TiRGN. If they ARE masked (filt excluded from the softmax), report this and fit two sensitivity variants on polecat TiRGN, CPU: UNMASKED (other true answers kept as negatives) and MULTIPOS (loss = -log sum_{true answers in pool} softmax over the unmasked pool). Comparison vs HRCOV_PAT re-fit in the same run; descriptive deltas with both CIs; no claim beyond the bounds."
 },
 "evaluator": "official py-tgb evaluator (hd_blend --no_controls over the promoted lists; TiRGN replay for polecat, stored float32 full rows for smallpedia); seed-mean per-query RR over seeds 0-2; H@k = mean over seeds",
 "statistics": {
  "query_bootstrap": "paired Poisson(1) bootstrap over test queries, B = 2000, seed 0 (hd_agg.boot)",
  "timestamp_block_bootstrap": "multinomial resampling of test timestamps (all queries of a timestamp, both directions), B = 2000, seed 0 (g7_cluster_bootstrap.boot_cluster); statistic = resampled sum of per-query deltas / resampled number of queries",
  "intervals": "two-sided 95% percentile CI from both bootstraps; one-sided 95% bounds L = 5th and U = 95th percentile",
  "positive_claim": "a difference is called present only if the one-sided lower bound L > 0 under BOTH bootstraps (Holm-adjusted one-sided p < 0.05 within an item when an item has several primary comparisons)",
  "null_claim": "an effect is called EXCLUDED (smaller than the bar) only if the one-sided upper bound U of the relevant signed delta < bar under the timestamp-block bootstrap (the more conservative); otherwise 'not excluded'. bar = 0.005 MRR unless stated",
  "MDE": "reported only as sensitivity: MDE_80 = (z_0.95 + z_0.80) x SE_ts = 2.486 x SE of the timestamp-block bootstrap; never used to support a null",
  "practical_margin": "0.005 MRR = the project's operational criterion (not a significance threshold)"
 },
 "interpretation": "Other true answers are already masked in Eq. (4) (code reading, A5); the two pre-specified sensitivity variants on polecat TiRGN change MRR by +0.00002 (UNMASKED) and -0.00034 (MULTIPOS); |delta| >= 0.005 is excluded for both, so the masking choice does not drive the result.",
 "notes": [
  "Fused arms: official = exact harness rank to <= 1e-7 MRR (hrank stored alongside rank).",
  "Score-alone arms (B_NF, NB_NF, EV_NF_*): official scoring orders the promoted list by the ranker score and breaks exact ties by list position (base top-50 order, then the generator block); the preliminary exact ranks used strict-greater (optimistic) ties. Difference official vs preliminary: polecat EV_NF_PT -0.00012, NB_NF -0.00006; smallpedia EV_NF_PT -0.00183, EV_NF_RB -0.00192, NB_NF -0.00011 (all other arms 0). The registered numbers are the official ones.",
  "Base replay: per-query base RR identical to the stored control/HRCOV_PAT files except near-tie blocks (polecat 0.011-0.012% of queries, mean |dRR| < 1e-8; smallpedia exactly identical).",
  "FULL re-fit vs stored HRCOV_PAT: smallpedia identical (deterministic CPU fit); polecat -0.00005, ts CI [-0.00017, +0.00006] (GPU fit).",
  "Run on polecat TiRGN only, as pre-specified. UNMASKED: other true same-timestamp answers kept as negatives in the listwise softmax; MULTIPOS: loss = -log sum over true answers in the pool of the softmax. Fit queries with >= 1 other true answer in top-50: polecat 20.0% (A5 code reading)."
 ],
